# Formal Russian: ты, вы and Нина Петровна
subtitle: "A knock at the door: Tom's new neighbour Нина Петровна, and how Russian says вы to strangers, older people and the boss, name and отчество included."
tags: ["russian","formal russian","ты and вы","patronymic","russian phrases"]
teaches: ["phrases/formal-register","phrases/greetings"]
thumb: "band \"Never call her ты\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Three plural endings in Russian: -ам, -ами, -ах","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/106-russian-plural-endings.cast"}

## Formal Russian: ты, вы and Нина Петровна
stress: all
level: basic
shuffle: true
heading: false

